From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 07:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] kernel: refuse to free a pointer outside the heap, and say who

MEM_TO_BHDR(ptr) computes a header address from the caller pointer and the
code reads it; a pointer that is not ours makes that a read of whatever the
arithmetic produced. Report the caller and decline.

Bounds are the area list, not mh_Lower/mh_Upper -- those describe only the
MemHeader the pool started from and TLSF adds areas beyond it. The first
version of this check used them and reported four legitimate frees per boot
as bad, declining them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/rom/kernel/tlsf.c
+++ b/rom/kernel/tlsf.c
@@ -670,6 +670,48 @@
     if (unlikely(!ptr))
         return;
 
+    /*
+     * [TLSF-BAD] Refuse to dereference a pointer that is in none of this
+     * heap's areas.
+     *
+     * MEM_TO_BHDR(ptr) computes a block header address from the caller's
+     * pointer and the code then reads it. A pointer that is not ours makes
+     * that a read of whatever the arithmetic produced. On the m68k-emu68 port
+     * those reads have been observed landing in unmapped space with values
+     * that are fragments of text -- a pointer variable holding string data at
+     * the moment it is freed. See AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0007.md.
+     *
+     * The bound is the area list, not mh_Lower/mh_Upper: those describe only
+     * the MemHeader this pool started from, and TLSF adds areas beyond it.
+     * Checking against them reports every allocation in an added area as bad,
+     * which is how the first version of this check produced four false
+     * positives per boot and, worse, declined four legitimate frees.
+     */
+    {
+        tlsf_area_t *a;
+        BOOL known = FALSE;
+
+        for (a = tlsf->memory_area; a != NULL; a = a->next)
+        {
+            /* An area runs from its own header to its end block. */
+            if ((APTR)ptr > (APTR)a && (APTR)ptr < (APTR)a->end)
+            {
+                known = TRUE;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+
+        if (!known)
+        {
+            static unsigned int tlsf_bad_seen;
+
+            if (tlsf_bad_seen++ < 16)
+                bug("[TLSF-BAD] free of %p in no area of this pool,"
+                    " caller %p\n", ptr, __builtin_return_address(0));
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+
     fb = MEM_TO_BHDR(ptr);
 
     BOOL sem_protected = !!(((ULONG)(IPTR)mhe->mhe_MemHeader.mh_First) & MEMF_SEM_PROTECTED);
